   "source": [
    "# 🎯 PS2 — Right-Party Contact (RPC) Prediction & Skip-Trace Prioritisation\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Goal:** For every phone number on file, predict whether it actually reaches the borrower, then decide: keep dialling, switch channel, or trigger a skip-trace.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Architecture Overview\n",
    "```\n",
    "Layer 1: STATE ESTIMATOR  →  \"What state is this contact point in?\"\n",
    "Layer 2: ACTION POLICY    →  \"Given all states, what should we do?\"\n",
    "Layer 3: TRACE VALUATION  →  \"Is it worth finding a new contact point?\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Contact-Point State Machine\n",
    "```\n",
    "valid → avoiding → switched_off → recycled → third_party → invalid\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Implementation Roadmap\n",
    "| Step | Module | Output |\n",
    "|------|--------|--------|\n",
    "| 0 | Data Loading & EDA | Schema understanding, null audit, baseline stats |\n",
    "| 1 | Label Engineering | RPC labels, state proxy labels |\n",
    "| 2 | Beta-Decay Baseline | Time-weighted Beta-Bernoulli RPC probability |\n",
    "| 3 | Avoiding vs Invalid GBDT | Hierarchical classifier (Stage A + B) |\n",
    "| 4 | Hazard Model + HMM | P(failure at t), filtered state posterior α_t |\n",
    "| 5 | Recycled-Number Detector | CUSUM + NLP suppression list |\n",
    "| 6 | Decision Table + EVT Skip-Trace | Action policy + EVT ranking |\n",
    "| 7 | Exploration (Thompson) + OPE | Safe policy evaluation |\n",
    "| 8 | Dashboard & Metrics | Final scorecard output |\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## ⚙️ Environment Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─── Core imports ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_columns', 50)\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_colwidth', 60)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ─── Visualisation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mtick\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import matplotlib.gridspec as gridspec\n",
    "from matplotlib.patches import FancyArrowPatch\n",
    "\n",
    "# Style\n",
    "plt.style.use('dark_background')\n",
    "PALETTE = ['#00D4FF', '#FF6B6B', '#FFE66D', '#A8E6CF', '#C3A6FF', '#FF8C42']\n",
    "sns.set_palette(PALETTE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ─── Paths ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import os\n",
    "BASE = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.getcwd()), 'OPEN_IIT', 'Dataset', 'data')\n",
    "# Adjust if needed:\n",
    "BASE = '/Users/adityagupta/Documents/OPEN_IIT/Dataset/data'\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'✅ Environment ready. BASE={BASE}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 📦 Step 0A — Data Loading\n",
    "\n",
    "We load all 9 tables relevant to PS2 and parse timestamps immediately so every subsequent step can work with proper datetime arithmetic."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─── Load all PS2-relevant tables ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "dial    = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/shared/dial_attempts.csv',            parse_dates=['attempt_ts'])\n",
    "phones  = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/ps2_right_party_contact/phones.csv', parse_dates=['added_date'])\n",
    "skips   = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/ps2_right_party_contact/skip_traces.csv', parse_dates=['trace_date'])\n",
    "vcp     = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/ps2_right_party_contact/verified_contact_points.csv', parse_dates=['verified_date'])\n",
    "visits  = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/shared/field_visits.csv',            parse_dates=['visit_date', 'start_ts', 'checkin_ts'])\n",
    "addrs   = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/shared/addresses.csv',               parse_dates=['added_date'])\n",
    "pmts    = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/shared/payments.csv',                parse_dates=['payment_ts'])\n",
    "accts   = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/shared/accounts.csv')\n",
    "agents  = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/shared/agents.csv')\n",
    "splits  = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE}/shared/splits.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ─── Quick size summary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "tables = {\n",
    "    'dial_attempts': dial, 'phones': phones, 'skip_traces': skips,\n",
    "    'verified_cp': vcp, 'field_visits': visits, 'addresses': addrs,\n",
    "    'payments': pmts, 'accounts': accts, 'agents': agents, 'splits': splits\n",
    "}\n",
    "print(f'{\"Table\":<25} {\"Rows\":>8} {\"Cols\":>6}')\n",
    "print('-'*42)\n",
    "for name, df in tables.items():\n",
    "    print(f'{name:<25} {len(df):>8,} {df.shape[1]:>6}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 📊 Step 0B — Null Audit\n",
    "\n",
    "Before any modelling, identify which columns carry missing values and at what rate. This drives imputation strategy later."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─── Null audit across all tables ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 5, figsize=(22, 8))\n",
    "axes = axes.flatten()\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, (name, df) in zip(axes, tables.items()):\n",
    "    null_pct = (df.isnull().mean() * 100).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    null_pct = null_pct[null_pct > 0]\n",
    "    if len(null_pct) == 0:\n",
    "        ax.text(0.5, 0.5, 'No nulls ✅', ha='center', va='center', color='#A8E6CF', fontsize=12)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(name, color='white', fontsize=9)\n",
    "        ax.axis('off')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        colors = ['#FF6B6B' if p > 30 else '#FFE66D' if p > 10 else '#00D4FF' for p in null_pct]\n",
    "        bars = ax.barh(null_pct.index, null_pct.values, color=colors)\n",
    "        ax.set_xlabel('% Null', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=8)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(name, color='white', fontsize=9)\n",
    "        ax.tick_params(axis='both', labelsize=7, colors='#AAAAAA')\n",
    "        ax.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "        for bar, val in zip(bars, null_pct.values):\n",
    "            ax.text(bar.get_width() + 0.5, bar.get_y() + bar.get_height()/2,\n",
    "                    f'{val:.1f}%', va='center', fontsize=6, color='white')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.patch.set_facecolor('#0d0d1a')\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Null Audit — All PS2 Tables', color='white', fontsize=14, y=1.01)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('null_audit.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight', facecolor=fig.get_facecolor())\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('✅ Null audit complete')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 📊 Step 0C — Dial Attempt EDA\n",
    "\n",
    "The dial attempts table is the engine of PS2. We analyse:\n",
    "- **Disposition distribution** — what outcomes actually happen?\n",
    "- **Network response** — layer beneath disposition\n",
    "- **Ring vs Talk duration** — signals for avoiding vs invalid\n",
    "- **Daily dial volume** — temporal dynamics\n",
    "- **Channel breakdown** — tele vs bot vs field"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─── Figure 1: Disposition & Network Response Distribution ─────────────────────\n",
    "fig = plt.figure(figsize=(20, 12), facecolor='#0d0d1a')\n",
    "gs = gridspec.GridSpec(2, 3, figure=fig, hspace=0.45, wspace=0.35)\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- 1A: Disposition bar chart\n",
    "ax1 = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 0])\n",
    "disp_counts = dial['disposition'].value_counts()\n",
    "colors_disp = [PALETTE[i % len(PALETTE)] for i in range(len(disp_counts))]\n",
    "bars = ax1.barh(disp_counts.index[::-1], disp_counts.values[::-1], color=colors_disp[::-1])\n",
    "ax1.set_title('Disposition Distribution\\n(51,105 attempts)', color='white', fontsize=11, pad=8)\n",
    "ax1.set_xlabel('Count', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax1.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=8)\n",
    "ax1.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "for bar in bars:\n",
    "    ax1.text(bar.get_width() + 50, bar.get_y() + bar.get_height()/2,\n",
    "             f'{bar.get_width():,.0f}', va='center', fontsize=7, color='white')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- 1B: Network response pie\n",
    "ax2 = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 1])\n",
    "nr = dial['network_response'].value_counts()\n",
    "wedge_props = dict(width=0.6, edgecolor='#0d0d1a', linewidth=2)\n",
    "ax2.pie(nr.values, labels=[l.replace('_', '\\n') for l in nr.index],\n",
    "        colors=PALETTE[:len(nr)], autopct='%1.1f%%', pctdistance=0.75,\n",
    "        textprops={'color': 'white', 'fontsize': 8}, wedgeprops=wedge_props)\n",
    "ax2.set_title('Network Response Breakdown', color='white', fontsize=11, pad=8)\n",
    "ax2.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- 1C: hangup_by\n",
    "ax3 = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, 2])\n",
    "hup = dial['hangup_by'].value_counts()\n",
    "ax3.bar(hup.index, hup.values, color=PALETTE[:len(hup)], edgecolor='#0d0d1a', linewidth=1.5)\n",
    "ax3.set_title('Hangup Initiator', color='white', fontsize=11, pad=8)\n",
    "ax3.set_ylabel('Count', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax3.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=9)\n",
    "ax3.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "for i, (val, bar_h) in enumerate(zip(hup.index, hup.values)):\n",
    "    ax3.text(i, bar_h + 200, f'{bar_h:,}', ha='center', fontsize=9, color='white')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- 1D: Ring duration distribution split by outcome group\n",
    "ax4 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 0])\n",
    "dial['outcome_group'] = dial['disposition'].map({\n",
    "    'rpc_ptp': 'RPC', 'rpc_hung_up': 'RPC', 'rpc_call_back': 'RPC',\n",
    "    'rpc_refused': 'RPC', 'rpc_hardship': 'RPC', 'rpc_dispute': 'RPC', 'rpc_claims_paid': 'RPC',\n",
    "    'no_answer': 'No Answer', 'call_rejected': 'Rejected',\n",
    "    'not_reachable': 'Not Reachable', 'switched_off': 'Switched Off',\n",
    "    'third_party_contact': 'Third Party', 'third_party_ptp': 'Third Party',\n",
    "    'wrong_number': 'Wrong/Invalid', 'invalid_number': 'Wrong/Invalid',\n",
    "    'language_barrier': 'RPC'\n",
    "})\n",
    "groups = ['RPC', 'No Answer', 'Rejected', 'Not Reachable', 'Switched Off', 'Third Party', 'Wrong/Invalid']\n",
    "ring_data = [dial[dial['outcome_group'] == g]['ring_duration_s'].dropna() for g in groups]\n",
    "bp = ax4.boxplot(ring_data, labels=groups, patch_artist=True, notch=False,\n",
    "                 medianprops=dict(color='white', linewidth=2))\n",
    "for patch, color in zip(bp['boxes'], PALETTE):\n",
    "    patch.set_facecolor(color)\n",
    "    patch.set_alpha(0.7)\n",
    "ax4.set_title('Ring Duration (s) by Outcome', color='white', fontsize=11, pad=8)\n",
    "ax4.set_ylabel('seconds', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax4.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=7)\n",
    "ax4.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "plt.setp(ax4.get_xticklabels(), rotation=30, ha='right')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- 1E: Talk duration by outcome (answered only)\n",
    "ax5 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 1])\n",
    "answered = dial[dial['talk_duration_s'] > 0].copy()\n",
    "talk_grps = answered.groupby('outcome_group')['talk_duration_s'].median().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "bars5 = ax5.bar(talk_grps.index, talk_grps.values, color=PALETTE[:len(talk_grps)], edgecolor='#0d0d1a')\n",
    "ax5.set_title('Median Talk Duration (s)\\n(answered calls only)', color='white', fontsize=11, pad=8)\n",
    "ax5.set_ylabel('seconds', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax5.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=8)\n",
    "ax5.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "plt.setp(ax5.get_xticklabels(), rotation=30, ha='right')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- 1F: channel breakdown\n",
    "ax6 = fig.add_subplot(gs[1, 2])\n",
    "ch_disp = dial.groupby(['channel', 'outcome_group']).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
    "ch_disp.plot(kind='bar', ax=ax6, stacked=True, color=PALETTE[:len(ch_disp.columns)],\n",
    "             edgecolor='#0d0d1a', linewidth=0.5)\n",
    "ax6.set_title('Outcome by Channel', color='white', fontsize=11, pad=8)\n",
    "ax6.set_ylabel('Attempts', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax6.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=9)\n",
    "ax6.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "ax6.legend(fontsize=7, framealpha=0.2, labelcolor='white')\n",
    "plt.setp(ax6.get_xticklabels(), rotation=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.patch.set_facecolor('#0d0d1a')\n",
    "plt.suptitle('PS2 — Dial Attempt Analysis', color='white', fontsize=15, y=1.01, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.savefig('dial_eda.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight', facecolor=fig.get_facecolor())\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('✅ Dial EDA complete')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 📊 Step 0D — Temporal Dynamics\n",
    "\n",
    "Understanding **when** dials happen and how outcomes evolve over time is critical for the hazard model (Step 4). We look at:\n",
    "- Daily call volume\n",
    "- RPC rate over time\n",
    "- Hour-of-day contact rate heatmap"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─── Temporal EDA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "dial['date'] = dial['attempt_ts'].dt.date\n",
    "dial['hour'] = dial['attempt_ts'].dt.hour\n",
    "dial['dow']  = dial['attempt_ts'].dt.day_name()\n",
    "dial['is_rpc'] = dial['disposition'].str.startswith('rpc').astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(20, 10), facecolor='#0d0d1a')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Daily volume\n",
    "ax = axes[0, 0]\n",
    "daily_vol = dial.groupby('date').size()\n",
    "ax.fill_between(range(len(daily_vol)), daily_vol.values, alpha=0.4, color='#00D4FF')\n",
    "ax.plot(range(len(daily_vol)), daily_vol.values, color='#00D4FF', linewidth=1.5)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Daily Dial Volume', color='white', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Day Index', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Attempts', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA')\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Daily RPC rate\n",
    "ax = axes[0, 1]\n",
    "daily_rpc = dial.groupby('date')['is_rpc'].mean() * 100\n",
    "ax.fill_between(range(len(daily_rpc)), daily_rpc.values, alpha=0.4, color='#FFE66D')\n",
    "ax.plot(range(len(daily_rpc)), daily_rpc.values, color='#FFE66D', linewidth=1.5)\n",
    "ax.axhline(daily_rpc.mean(), color='#FF6B6B', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5,\n",
    "           label=f'Mean={daily_rpc.mean():.1f}%')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Daily RPC Rate (%)', color='white', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Day Index', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('RPC %', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA')\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=9, framealpha=0.2, labelcolor='white')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Hourly contact heatmap (hour x DOW)\n",
    "ax = axes[1, 0]\n",
    "DOW_ORDER = ['Monday', 'Tuesday', 'Wednesday', 'Thursday', 'Friday', 'Saturday', 'Sunday']\n",
    "heatmap_data = dial.groupby(['dow', 'hour'])['is_rpc'].mean().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
    "heatmap_data = heatmap_data.reindex([d for d in DOW_ORDER if d in heatmap_data.index])\n",
    "sns.heatmap(heatmap_data, ax=ax, cmap='YlOrRd', linewidths=0.3, linecolor='#0d0d1a',\n",
    "            cbar_kws={'shrink': 0.8, 'label': 'RPC Rate'},\n",
    "            annot=False)\n",
    "ax.set_title('RPC Rate by Day × Hour', color='white', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Hour of Day', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=8)\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Attempts-per-phone distribution\n",
    "ax = axes[1, 1]\n",
    "attempts_per_phone = dial.groupby('phone_id').size()\n",
    "ax.hist(attempts_per_phone.clip(upper=50), bins=50, color='#C3A6FF', edgecolor='#0d0d1a', linewidth=0.5)\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'Attempts per Phone (n={len(attempts_per_phone):,} phones)\\nclipped at 50', color='white', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('# Attempts', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('# Phones', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA')\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "median_v = attempts_per_phone.median()\n",
    "ax.axvline(median_v, color='#FFE66D', linestyle='--', label=f'Median={median_v:.0f}')\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=9, framealpha=0.2, labelcolor='white')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.patch.set_facecolor('#0d0d1a')\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Temporal & Volume Dynamics', color='white', fontsize=15, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('temporal_eda.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight', facecolor=fig.get_facecolor())\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print('✅ Temporal EDA complete')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 📊 Step 0E — Phone Portfolio EDA\n",
    "\n",
    "Analyse the phone number inventory: source diversity, relation types, priority slot distribution, and link to accounts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─── Phone portfolio analysis ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(20, 6), facecolor='#0d0d1a')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Source breakdown\n",
    "ax = axes[0]\n",
    "src = phones['source'].value_counts()\n",
    "wedge_props = dict(width=0.55, edgecolor='#0d0d1a', linewidth=2)\n",
    "ax.pie(src.values, labels=src.index, colors=PALETTE[:len(src)],\n",
    "       autopct='%1.1f%%', pctdistance=0.7, textprops={'color': 'white', 'fontsize': 9},\n",
    "       wedgeprops=wedge_props)\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'Phone Source ({len(phones):,} numbers)', color='white', fontsize=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Relation type\n",
    "ax = axes[1]\n",
    "rel = phones['relation_recorded'].value_counts()\n",
    "bars = ax.barh(rel.index[::-1], rel.values[::-1], color=PALETTE[:len(rel)])\n",
    "ax.set_title('Relation Recorded', color='white', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "for bar in bars:\n",
    "    ax.text(bar.get_width() + 5, bar.get_y() + bar.get_height()/2,\n",
    "            f'{bar.get_width():,}', va='center', fontsize=8, color='white')\n",
    "\n",
    "# -- Phones per account distribution\n",
    "ax = axes[2]\n",
    "phones_per_acct = phones.groupby('account_id').size().value_counts().sort_index()\n",
    "ax.bar(phones_per_acct.index.astype(str), phones_per_acct.values,\n",
    "       color=PALETTE[2], edgecolor='#0d0d1a', linewidth=1)\n",
    "ax.set_title('# Phones per Account', color='white', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('# Phone Numbers', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('# Accounts', color='#AAAAAA', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.tick_params(colors='#AAAAAA', labelsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor('#1a1a2e')\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(phones_per_acct.values):\n",
    "    ax.text(i, v + 5, str(v), ha='center', fontsize=9, color='white')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.patch.set_facecolor('#0d0d1a')\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Phone Portfolio Overview', color='white', fontsize=15, fontweight='bold')\n",
