    "---\n",
    "## 🎲 Step 7 — Exploration Layer + Off-Policy Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Thompson Sampling Exploration\n",
    "Reserve **2-5% of dialling budget** for exploration — trying phones the policy would otherwise skip. This prevents the model from getting stuck in local optima.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hard constraint:** Never explore on **suppressed** numbers.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Off-Policy Evaluation (OPE)\n",
    "Use **Doubly Robust (DR) estimator** to evaluate a new policy against logged data — without deploying it live first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─── Step 7: Thompson Sampling + OPE ───────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ─── 7A: Thompson Sampling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# For each non-suppressed phone, sample θ ~ Beta(α_post, β_post)\n",
    "# Select phones with highest sampled θ for exploration budget\n",
    "\n",
    "explore_pool = scorecard[\n",
    "    (~scorecard['suppressed']) &\n",
    "    (scorecard['action'].isin(['RETRY_48H', 'SWITCH_CHANNEL']))\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "explore_pool = explore_pool.merge(\n",
    "    phone_scores[['phone_id', 'alpha_post', 'beta_post']], on='phone_id', how='left'\n",
    ")\n",
    "explore_pool['alpha_post'] = explore_pool['alpha_post'].fillna(1.0)\n",
    "explore_pool['beta_post']  = explore_pool['beta_post'].fillna(3.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Thompson sample\n",
    "explore_pool['ts_sample'] = np.random.beta(\n",
    "    explore_pool['alpha_post'].values,\n",
    "    explore_pool['beta_post'].values\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "EXPLORE_BUDGET = int(0.03 * len(scorecard[scorecard['action'] == 'DIAL']))  # 3% of DIAL actions\n",
    "explore_selected = explore_pool.nlargest(EXPLORE_BUDGET, 'ts_sample')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Exploration budget:    {EXPLORE_BUDGET} phones (3% of DIAL)')\n",
    "print(f'Thompson pool size:    {len(explore_pool):,}')\n",
    "print(f'Selected for explore:  {len(explore_selected):,}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ─── 7B: Doubly Robust OPE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# We simulate comparing \"rule-based\" (current) vs \"model-based\" (new) policy\n",
    "# using logged dial attempts as the offline dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Logged propensity (selection_propensity from data)\n",
    "dial_ope = dial2.copy()\n",
    "dial_ope['pi_b'] = dial_ope['selection_propensity'].clip(lower=0.01)  # behavior policy\n",
    "\n",
    "# New policy: phones with P(RPC) > 0.3\n",
    "dial_ope = dial_ope.merge(phone_scores[['phone_id', 'p_rpc_beta']], on='phone_id', how='left')\n",
    "dial_ope['pi_e'] = (dial_ope['p_rpc_beta'] > 0.30).astype(float).clip(lower=0.01)  # evaluation policy\n",
    "\n",
    "# Reward: RPC indicator\n",
    "reward = dial_ope['is_rpc'].values\n",
    "pi_b   = dial_ope['pi_b'].values\n",
    "pi_e   = dial_ope['pi_e'].values\n",
    "p_hat  = dial_ope['p_rpc_beta'].values  # model estimate\n",
    "\n",
    "# IPS estimate\n",
    "ips_weights = pi_e / pi_b\n",
    "ips_weights = np.clip(ips_weights, 0, 5)  # clip for stability\n",
    "IPS_estimate = (ips_weights * reward).mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "# DR estimate\n",
    "DR_estimate = p_hat.mean() + (ips_weights * (reward - p_hat)).mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "baseline_rpc = reward.mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\n=== Off-Policy Evaluation ===')\n",
    "print(f'Baseline RPC rate (rule-based):  {baseline_rpc:.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'IPS estimate (new policy):       {IPS_estimate:.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'DR estimate (new policy):        {DR_estimate:.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'Estimated improvement (DR):      {(DR_estimate - baseline_rpc) / baseline_rpc:+.1%}')"
   ]
  },
